  "description": "Each record is `[student_name, score]`. Use a `GradeBook` class to collect scores and return a dictionary mapping each student to their average score. Keep insertion-independent dictionary results and return `{}` for no records.",
  "starterCode": "def grade_report(records):\n    # Return average score per student using a GradeBook class\n    pass\n",
  "referenceSolution": "class GradeBook:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.scores = {}\n\n    def add(self, name, score):\n        self.scores.setdefault(name, []).append(score)\n\n    def averages(self):\n        return {name: sum(values) / len(values) for name, values in self.scores.items()}\n\ndef grade_report(records):\n    book = GradeBook()\n    for name, score in records:\n        book.add(name, score)\n    return book.averages()",
  "solution": {
    "code": "class GradeBook:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.scores = {}\n\n    def add(self, name, score):\n        self.scores.setdefault(name, []).append(score)\n\n    def averages(self):\n        return {name: sum(values) / len(values) for name, values in self.scores.items()}\n\ndef grade_report(records):\n    book = GradeBook()\n    for name, score in records:\n        book.add(name, score)\n    return book.averages()",
    "explanation": "A small GradeBook class owns each student’s list of grades and calculates its average. The wrapper adds records to the book and returns a report dictionary. Empty input produces an empty report, and repeated students share one record."
  },
  "wrongSolutions": [
    "def grade_report(records):\n    return {name:score for name,score in records}",
    "def grade_report(records):\n    return {name:sum(score for n,score in records if n==name) for name,score in records}"
  ],
